# Production FastAPI & Clean Architecture Standards

This skill provides comprehensive architectural patterns, typing practices, and production engineering standards for building scalable, asynchronous microservices using **FastAPI**, **Pydantic v2**, **SQLAlchemy 2.0 / asyncpg**, and **Pytest**.

---

## 1. Clean Architecture Project Layout

Enforce strict layer boundaries and Dependency Inversion:

```
src/
├── api/                   # Presentation Layer (FastAPI Routers, Middleware, Dependencies)
│   ├── v1/
│   │   ├── endpoints/     # HTTP route handlers
│   │   └── router.py      # Aggregated v1 APIRouter
│   └── dependencies.py    # Common DI providers (Auth, DB session, Repositories)
├── core/                  # Configuration & Cross-Cutting Concerns
│   ├── config.py          # Pydantic-settings BaseSettings
│   ├── logging.py         # Structlog / Loguru structured logging
│   └── security.py        # Token generation, password hashing
├── domain/                # Core Business Entities & Interfaces
│   ├── models/            # Pure dataclasses or domain models
│   └── ports/             # Abstract Repository / Service interfaces (Protocols)
├── infrastructure/        # External Implementations
│   ├── db/                # SQLAlchemy models, migrations, engine, sessions
│   ├── repositories/      # Concrete repository implementations
│   └── clients/           # External API & Scraper clients (Playwright, HTTPX)
├── application/           # Use Cases & Orchestration Services
│   ├── services/          # Business logic coordinators
│   └── dtos/              # Application-level data transfer objects
└── main.py                # App factory & Lifespan handler
```

---

## 2. FastAPI Lifespan & Clean Dependency Injection

```python
from contextlib import asynccontextmanager
from typing import AsyncGenerator
from fastapi import FastAPI, Depends, HTTPException, status
from pydantic_settings import BaseSettings
import structlog

logger = structlog.get_logger()

@asynccontextmanager
async def lifespan(app: FastAPI):
    logger.info("service_startup", status="initializing_resources")
    # Initialize DB connection pools, Redis clients, or browser contexts
    yield
    logger.info("service_shutdown", status="cleaning_up_resources")
    # Graceful connection closure

app = FastAPI(title="BestStart Microservice", lifespan=lifespan)
```

---

## 3. Pydantic v2 Production Schemas & Validation

Always use Pydantic v2 `ConfigDict` and typed annotations:

```python
from typing import Annotated, Optional
from datetime import datetime
from pydantic import BaseModel, ConfigDict, Field, field_validator, StringConstraints

NonEmptyStr = Annotated[str, StringConstraints(strip_whitespace=True, min_length=1)]

class BaseSchema(BaseModel):
    model_config = ConfigDict(
        from_attributes=True,
        populate_by_name=True,
        extra="forbid",
        str_strip_whitespace=True,
    )

class UserCreateRequest(BaseSchema):
    email: NonEmptyStr = Field(..., example="operator@beststart.local")
    username: NonEmptyStr = Field(..., max_length=64)
    role: str = Field(default="analyst")

    @field_validator("email")
    @classmethod
    def validate_email_domain(cls, v: str) -> str:
        if "@" not in v or "." not in v.split("@")[-1]:
            raise ValueError("Invalid email format")
        return v.lower()

class UserResponse(BaseSchema):
    id: int
    email: str
    username: str
    is_active: bool
    created_at: datetime
```

